//   the practical arrangements — scheduling, format, frequency of
//   the examinations — are agreed with the local (rayon/city)
//   education authorities. We say so plainly, help families
//   document, and never promise a smoothness we cannot verify.
//   Never overclaim procedural detail beyond: legal form, state
//   standards, MoE-supervised examinations, local arrangement.
// - THE WINDOW: compulsory education is GENERAL SECONDARY — nine
//   years, grades 1-9, roughly ages 6-15 (Constitution Art. 42).
//   FULL SECONDARY (grades 10-11) IS NOT COMPULSORY. The A-Level
//   years after grade 9 sit outside the obligation — the
//   Hungary/Greece-style wedge, used prominently and honestly.
